\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
The efficient price process 
\begin_inset Formula $X_{t}$
\end_inset

 is described by:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\frac{dX_{t}}{X_{t}}=\mu_{t}dt+\sigma_{t}dW_{t}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\omega_{t}=\mu_{t}-\frac{1}{2}\sigma_{t}^{2}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For the 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu=0$
\end_inset

 case we have (RR2009):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{\eta}=\sum_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}\cdot u_{k}\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\lambda_{k}=\frac{N_{k}^{A}+N_{k}^{C}}{\sum_{k}\left(N_{k}^{A}+N_{k}^{C}\right)}
\]

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
u_{k}=\frac{k\cdot N_{k}^{C}}{2\cdot N_{k}^{A}}-\left(\frac{k-1}{2}\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Frame

\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Separator parbreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame
\begin_inset Argument 4
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Conditional CDFs
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Conditional durations (
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta t$
\end_inset

 to next price change) are described by (the sign 
\begin_inset Formula $\pm$
\end_inset

 refers to ud):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
P_{\pm}\left(t\right)= & +e^{\frac{\omega}{\sigma^{2}}\cdot\left(b_{1}-x_{0}\right)}\cdot\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\left\{ e^{\frac{\omega}{\sigma^{2}}\cdot y_{n}^{\pm}}\cdot N\left(\frac{y_{n}^{\pm}+\omega\cdot t}{\sigma\cdot\sqrt{t}}\right)+e^{-\frac{\omega}{\sigma^{2}}\cdot y_{n}^{\pm}}N\left(\frac{y_{n}^{\pm}-\omega\cdot t}{\sigma\cdot\sqrt{t}}\right)\right\} \\
 & -e^{\frac{\omega}{\sigma^{2}}\cdot\left(b_{1}-x_{0}\right)}\cdot\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\left\{ e^{\frac{\omega}{\sigma^{2}}\cdot z_{n}^{\pm}}\cdot N\left(\frac{z_{n}^{\pm}+\omega\cdot t}{\sigma\cdot\sqrt{t}}\right)+e^{-\frac{\omega}{\sigma^{2}}\cdot z_{n}^{\pm}}\cdot N\left(\frac{z_{n}^{\pm}-\omega\cdot t}{\sigma\cdot\sqrt{t}}\right)\right\} 
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula $b_{1}=Log[S_{0}+ud\cdot\left(\frac{1}{2}+\eta\right)\cdot\alpha]$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula $b_{2}=Log[S_{0}-ud\cdot\left(\frac{1}{2}+\eta\right)\cdot\alpha]$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula $x_{0}=Log[S_{0}+sud\cdot\left(\frac{1}{2}+\eta\right)\cdot\alpha]$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula $y_{1}=+ud\cdot\left(x_{0}-b_{1}\right)<0$
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula $y_{n}=y_{1}+ud\cdot2\cdot\left(n-1\right)\cdot\left(b_{2}-b_{1}\right)<y_{1}$
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula $z_{n}=y_{n}+ud\cdot2\cdot\left(b_{2}-x_{0}\right)<y_{n}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Separator parbreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame
\begin_inset Argument 4
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
To infinity ...
 and beyond
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
The limits for 
\begin_inset Formula $t\rightarrow\infty$
\end_inset

 are:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
P_{\pm}\left(\omega\neq0\right)= & e^{\left(\frac{1-sign[\omega]\cdot ud}{2}\right)\cdot\left(b_{1}-x_{0}\right)}\cdot\left(\frac{1-e^{\left(\frac{2\cdot abs[\omega]\cdot ud}{\sigma^{2}}\right)\cdot\left(b_{2}-x_{0}\right)}}{1-e^{\left(\frac{2\cdot abs[\omega]\cdot ud}{\sigma^{2}}\right)\cdot\left(b_{2}-b_{1}\right)}}\right)\\
P_{\pm}\left(\omega=0\right)= & \frac{b_{2}-x_{0}}{b_{2}-b_{1}}
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
So given the sign of the last trade: 
\begin_inset Formula $sud_{j}=-ud_{j-1}$
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
We know 
\begin_inset Formula $S_{0}+sud\left(\frac{1}{2}-\eta\right)\cdot\alpha$
\end_inset

 and the probabilities of an up or down move
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
And based on which move happens we know the CDF of the durations
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Separator parbreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame
\begin_inset Argument 4
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Logistic approximation
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
The formulas from the previous slide for continuations can be approximated
 by:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\size footnotesize
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
P_{\pm}^{C}= & \left(\frac{2\cdot\eta}{1+2\cdot\eta}\right)\cdot\left(\frac{2}{1+e^{\left(\mp2\cdot\frac{\mu}{\sigma^{2}}\cdot\frac{\alpha}{S_{0}}\right)}}\right)\\
P_{\mp}^{A}= & 1-P_{\pm}^{C}
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
And average durations can be estimated by defining a scale 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau$
\end_inset

: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\tau=2\cdot\eta\cdot\left(\frac{\alpha}{\sigma\cdot S}\right)^{2}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
For the 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu=0$
\end_inset

 case the average conditional durations are:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\tau^{A}=\frac{2+2\cdot\eta}{3}\cdot\tau
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\tau^{C}=\frac{1+4\cdot\eta}{6\cdot\eta}\cdot\tau
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Separator parbreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame
\begin_inset Argument 4
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The trend is not a friend
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
For the 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu\neq0$
\end_inset

 case the average duration gets modified (reduced) by a factor that is close
 to:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
adj_{\tau}=\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{\mu}{2\sqrt{2}\cdot\sigma}\right)^{2}\cdot\left(\frac{\alpha}{\sigma\cdot S}\right)^{2}}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Later when we use the distribution of the durations for inference we will
 see that we benefit from looking at the cases where 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu\neq0$
\end_inset

 , as 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{\partial\left(\tau\cdot adj_{\tau}\right)}{\partial\mu}=0$
\end_inset

 at 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu=0$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Separator parbreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame
\begin_inset Argument 4
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Large moves
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Continuations of k ticks:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
P\left(k,\alpha,\eta,t\right)\rightarrow P\left(1,k\cdot\alpha,\frac{\eta}{k},t\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Alternations of k ticks:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
P\left(k,\alpha,\eta,t\right)\rightarrow P\left(1,\alpha,\eta+\left(\frac{k-1}{2}\right),t\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
This is a really good way of dealing with these moves later with the bayesian
 estimator
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Separator parbreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Frame
\begin_inset Argument 4
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Updated estimator
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset Separator latexpar
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
We can write:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{\eta}=\frac{\sum_{k}\left(k\cdot N_{k}^{C}\right)}{2\cdot\sum_{k}\left(N_{k}^{A}\right)}-\sum_{k}\left(\lambda_{k}\cdot\left(\frac{k-1}{2}\right)\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
With
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\lambda_{k}=\frac{N_{k}^{A}}{\sum_{k}\left(N_{k}^{A}\right)}
