\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
How did we update μ after 20 price changes?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The likelihood 
\begin_inset Formula $p\left(x\;\middle\vert\;\theta\right)$
\end_inset

 is given by the multinomial likelihood:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Formula $p\left(\left\{ n_{+}^{A},n_{-}^{A},n_{+}^{C},n_{-}^{C}\right\} \;\middle\vert\;\left\{ \rho_{+}^{A},\rho_{-}^{A},\rho_{+}^{C},\rho_{-}^{C}\right\} \right)=\frac{\left(n_{+}^{A}+n_{-}^{A}+n_{+}^{C}+n_{-}^{C}\right)!}{\left(n_{+}^{A}!\cdot n_{-}^{A}!\cdot n_{+}^{C}!\cdot n_{-}^{C}!\right)}\left(\left(\rho_{+}^{A}\right)^{n_{+}^{A}}\cdot\left(\rho_{-}^{A}\right)^{n_{-}^{A}}\cdot\left(\rho_{+}^{C}\right)^{n_{+}^{C}}\cdot\left(\rho_{-}^{C}\right)^{n_{-}^{C}}\right)$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Two different goals: (i) Historical / EOD and (ii) Online (our focus)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
For Historical we can get a large window (e.g.
 n=100) and use the posterior for μ back to recalculate θ (until it doesn't
 change)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
For Online we try to choose n that is big enough to give us some differentiation
 but not that big that will take too long to update or that will give us
 a likelihood too narrow
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
We can use n=20 up to n=50; with n=20 we're bound to react too quickly,
 but updating the probabilities every 20 changes as well should be enough
 to dissipate transients quite quickly
\end_layout

\end_deeper
